<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Concepción, Chile</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Concepción is a city in south-central Chile near the mouth of the Biobío river, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia">Pedro de Valdivia</a> in 1550. As the main Spanish base on the frontier of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a> it housed the colony's army. After an earthquake and tsunami destroyed it in 1751, it was rebuilt at its present site; it is now one of Chile's largest cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/concepcion-chile.jpg" alt="Concepción, Chile" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gherm · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arco_de_medicina_Udec.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
